SRR31168300	PRJNA1179956	SRP542128	SAMN44510294	SRX26551695	Homo sapiens	SBC5_SH2	SBC5_SH2	Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM8603681: SBC5_SH2 Homo sapiens ATAC-seq	ATAC-seq	GENOMIC	other	PAIRED	ILLUMINA	Illumina NovaSeq 6000	For each submitted sample, 60 000 viable cells were pelleted at 500 x g for 5 minutes at 4oC, resuspended in 50 µL of fully supplemented ATAC-seq resuspension buffer (RSB) containing 0.1% NP-40, 0.1% Tween-20, and 0.01% digitonin, and incubated on ice for 3 minutes. Following lysis, 1 mL of ATAC-seq RSB containing 0.1% Tween-20 (without NP-40 or digitonin) was added and the tubes were inverted to mix. Nuclei were then centrifuged at 500 x g for 10 minutes at 4oC, followed by careful aspiration of all supernatant and resuspension of pellet with 50 µL of transposition master mix (25 µL 2x TD buffer, 2.5 µL transposase, 16.5 µL PBS, 0.5 µL 1% digitonin, 0.5 µL 10% Tween-20, and 5 µL water). Transposition reactions were incubated at 37oC for 30 minutes in a thermomixer with shaking at 1000 rpm. Reactions were cleaned up with MinElute columns (Qiagen, catalog # 28204), followed by library amplification, where the appropriate number of PCR cycles was determined by qPCR. PCR product purification and size selection were achieved using AMPure XP Beads (Beckman Coulter, catalog # A63882).	60056254	6125737908	ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR311/000/SRR31168300/SRR31168300_1.fastq.gz;ftp.sra.ebi.ac.uk/vol1/fastq/SRR311/000/SRR31168300/SRR31168300_2.fastq.gz	a860603120879cb1b2c37bc298635bd8;2b166e56eac30ad74d4fb7593357c287	1941726713;1892562078
